-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part I, Division B -- sections 16 to 20: THE MAXIMUMS AND THE EXEMPTION.
--
-- Sections 18, 18.1 and 20 fix, for a year, the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings, the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable
-- Earnings and the Year's Basic Exemption. Sections 17, 17.1 and 19 give a person's own maximum pensionable earnings, additional
-- maximum and basic exemption for a year: the Year's figure, prorated by months in a year in which the person reaches
-- eighteen or seventy, dies, leaves the contributory period or stops receiving a disability pension, or elects. Section 16
-- is the person's maximum contributory earnings: the maximum pensionable earnings less the basic exemption.
--
-- The Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for 1988 on is a ratio of Wage Measure averages published by Statistics Canada,
-- which the text does not contain: the averages are plain inputs. The text states one figure itself, 25,900 dollars for 1987.
--
-- out of range: Statistics Canada's published Wage Measure is not part of this text (subsection 18(5) names it): the twelve month averages are plain inputs.
-- out of range: regulation 85 (piece cr1): the time of calculation and the rounding of the averages and the ratio (to two and four decimal places); the inputs are taken as already rounded.
-- out of range: the advice of the Chief Statistician, in subsections 18(7) and (8), is not part of this text: the Minister's adjustment is a plain input.
-- out of range: section 49 (piece cp3), section 70 (piece cp5), sections 44 and 67 (pieces cp3 and cp5): the contributory period and the retirement pension, as for section 12.
--
-- Ages go through the keel's section 2(2) rules. Paragraphs 17(c), 17.1(c), 19(c) and 19(d) are among the ten places where
-- the actual birthday governs (constructors `paragraph 17(c)`, `paragraph 17.1(c)`, `paragraph 19(c)`, `paragraph 19(d)`);
-- paragraphs (a) and (b) of the three sections are not.
--
-- Subsections 8(6), (7), (10) and (11) ask for these figures "determined without taking into account" paragraphs (b) and
-- (c): each of sections 17, 17.1 and 19 has a second rule for that.

§ `Division B -- Calculation of Contributions`

§§ `Section 18 -- the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings`

-- src:516 | Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings
-- src:517 | Amount of Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings
-- src:518 | 18 (1) The amount of a Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings is
-- src:519 | (a) for 1987, $25,900;
-- src:520 | (b) subject to subsection (2), for 1988, an amount calculated by multiplying the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for 1987 by the ratio that
-- src:521 | (i) the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30, 1987 of the Wage Measure for each month in that period
-- src:522 | bears to
-- src:523 | (ii) the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30, 1986 of the Wage Measure for each month in that period; and
-- src:524 | (c) subject to subsection (2), for 1989 and each subsequent year, an amount calculated by multiplying the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the preceding year, calculated without reference to subsections (2) and (3), by the ratio that
-- src:525 | (i) the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30 of the preceding year of the Wage Measure for each month in that period
-- src:526 | bears to
-- src:527 | (ii) the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30 of the year immediately preceding the preceding year of the Wage Measure for each month in that period.
@ref Act s 18(1)(a) (src:519)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 18(1)(a) — the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for 1987` MEANS 25_900

@ref Act s 18(1)(b) (src:520-523)
GIVEN `the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30, 1987 of the Wage Measure for each month in that period` IS A NUMBER
      `the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30, 1986 of the Wage Measure for each month in that period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 18(1)(b) — the amount calculated for 1988` `the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30, 1987 of the Wage Measure for each month in that period` `the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30, 1986 of the Wage Measure for each month in that period` MEANS
    IF `the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30, 1986 of the Wage Measure for each month in that period` EQUALS 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`s 18(1)(a) — the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for 1987`
               TIMES `the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30, 1987 of the Wage Measure for each month in that period`
               DIVIDED BY `the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30, 1986 of the Wage Measure for each month in that period`)

@ref Act s 18(1)(c) (src:524-527)
GIVEN `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the preceding year, calculated without reference to subsections (2) and (3)` IS A NUMBER
      `the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30 of the preceding year of the Wage Measure for each month in that period` IS A NUMBER
      `the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30 of the year immediately preceding the preceding year of the Wage Measure for each month in that period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 18(1)(c) — the amount calculated for 1989 and each subsequent year` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the preceding year, calculated without reference to subsections (2) and (3)` `the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30 of the preceding year of the Wage Measure for each month in that period` `the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30 of the year immediately preceding the preceding year of the Wage Measure for each month in that period` MEANS
    IF `the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30 of the year immediately preceding the preceding year of the Wage Measure for each month in that period` EQUALS 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the preceding year, calculated without reference to subsections (2) and (3)`
               TIMES `the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30 of the preceding year of the Wage Measure for each month in that period`
               DIVIDED BY `the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30 of the year immediately preceding the preceding year of the Wage Measure for each month in that period`)

-- The amount calculated for a year under paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c): 1987 is the stated figure, 1988 uses paragraph (b),
-- every later year paragraph (c). The Wage Measure averages are the two of the preceding twelve-month periods ending June 30
-- (for 1988: June 30, 1987 and June 30, 1986). Before 1987 the text gives nothing (NOTHING).
@ref Act s 18(1) (src:517-527)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the preceding year, calculated without reference to subsections (2) and (3)` IS A NUMBER
      `the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30 of the preceding year of the Wage Measure for each month in that period` IS A NUMBER
      `the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30 of the year immediately preceding the preceding year of the Wage Measure for each month in that period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 18(1) — the amount calculated for a year` year `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the preceding year, calculated without reference to subsections (2) and (3)` `the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30 of the preceding year of the Wage Measure for each month in that period` `the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30 of the year immediately preceding the preceding year of the Wage Measure for each month in that period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF year LESS THAN 1987 THEN NOTHING
        IF year EQUALS 1987 THEN JUST `s 18(1)(a) — the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for 1987`
        IF year EQUALS 1988
        THEN `s 18(1)(b) — the amount calculated for 1988`
                 `the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30 of the preceding year of the Wage Measure for each month in that period`
                 `the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30 of the year immediately preceding the preceding year of the Wage Measure for each month in that period`
        OTHERWISE
            `s 18(1)(c) — the amount calculated for 1989 and each subsequent year`
                `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the preceding year, calculated without reference to subsections (2) and (3)`
                `the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30 of the preceding year of the Wage Measure for each month in that period`
                `the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30 of the year immediately preceding the preceding year of the Wage Measure for each month in that period`

-- src:528 | Rounding off
-- src:529 | (2) Where the amount calculated in accordance with paragraph (1)(b) or (c) for any year is not a multiple of one hundred dollars, the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year is the amount that is the next multiple of one hundred dollars below that amount.
-- src:530 | Minimum amount of Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings
-- src:531 | (3) Where the amount calculated in accordance with paragraph (1)(b) or (c) in respect of any year is less than the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the preceding year, it shall be increased to the amount of the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the preceding year.
@ref Act s 18(2) (src:528-529)
GIVEN `the amount calculated in accordance with paragraph (1)(b) or (c)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 18(2) — the amount rounded down to a multiple of one hundred dollars` `the amount calculated in accordance with paragraph (1)(b) or (c)` MEANS
    (FLOOR (`the amount calculated in accordance with paragraph (1)(b) or (c)` DIVIDED BY 100)) TIMES 100

-- Increased to the preceding year's amount where the calculated amount is less than it. NOTHING: the calculated amount is not less.
@ref Act s 18(3) (src:530-531)
GIVEN `the amount calculated in accordance with paragraph (1)(b) or (c)` IS A NUMBER
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the preceding year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 18(3) — the amount the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings is increased to` `the amount calculated in accordance with paragraph (1)(b) or (c)` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the preceding year` MEANS
    IF `the amount calculated in accordance with paragraph (1)(b) or (c)` LESS THAN `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the preceding year`
    THEN JUST `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the preceding year`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The amount of a Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings from 1988: rounded down (2), or raised to the preceding year's amount (3).
-- 1987 is the amount stated in (1)(a); before 1987 the text gives nothing (NOTHING).
@ref Act s 18(1) (src:517-531)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the amount calculated in accordance with paragraph (1)(b) or (c)` IS A NUMBER
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the preceding year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 18 — the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` year `the amount calculated in accordance with paragraph (1)(b) or (c)` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the preceding year` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF year LESS THAN 1987 THEN NOTHING
        IF year EQUALS 1987 THEN JUST `s 18(1)(a) — the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for 1987`
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `s 18(3) — the amount the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings is increased to` `the amount calculated in accordance with paragraph (1)(b) or (c)` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the preceding year`
            WHEN JUST increased THEN JUST increased
            WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (`s 18(2) — the amount rounded down to a multiple of one hundred dollars` `the amount calculated in accordance with paragraph (1)(b) or (c)`)

-- Subsection 18(4) (Act line 532) reads "[Repealed, 1991, c. 44, s. 2]" in this text; there is nothing to encode (NOTES.md, coverage table).

-- src:533 | Wage Measure
-- src:534 | (5) The Wage Measure for a month is the average weekly wages and salaries of
-- src:535 | (a) the Industrial Aggregate in Canada for the month as published by Statistics Canada under the authority of the Statistics Act; or
-- src:536 | (b) in the event that the Industrial Aggregate ceases to be published, such other measure as is prescribed by regulation for the month as published by Statistics Canada under the authority of the Statistics Act.
@ref Act s 18(5) (src:534-536)
GIVEN `the Industrial Aggregate in Canada is published by Statistics Canada for the month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the average weekly wages and salaries of the Industrial Aggregate in Canada for the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the average weekly wages and salaries of the other measure prescribed by regulation for the month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 18(5) — the Wage Measure for a month` `the Industrial Aggregate in Canada is published by Statistics Canada for the month` `the average weekly wages and salaries of the Industrial Aggregate in Canada for the month` `the average weekly wages and salaries of the other measure prescribed by regulation for the month` MEANS
    -- (a) the Industrial Aggregate; (b) in the event that it ceases to be published, the other measure prescribed by regulation
    IF `the Industrial Aggregate in Canada is published by Statistics Canada for the month`
    THEN `the average weekly wages and salaries of the Industrial Aggregate in Canada for the month`
    ELSE `the average weekly wages and salaries of the other measure prescribed by regulation for the month`

-- src:537 | Idem
-- src:538 | (6) For the purpose of calculating the amount of a Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings, where Statistics Canada has published any revisions of the Industrial Aggregate or the other measure referred to in paragraph (5)(b) for any month, the revision of the Industrial Aggregate or the other measure referred to in paragraph (5)(b) that has been published most recently prior to the calculation in respect of that month shall be used in calculating the amount of the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings.
-- The revision "that has been published most recently prior to the calculation". NOTHING: none had been published before it.
@ref Act s 18(6) (src:537-538)
GIVEN revisions IS A LIST OF `cp1 Published figure`
      `date of the calculation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 18(6) — the revision of the Wage Measure published most recently prior to the calculation` revisions `date of the calculation` MEANS
    IF null `revisions published before the calculation`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST ((at `those published on the latest day` (count `those published on the latest day` MINUS 1))'s `the published figure`)
    WHERE
        `revisions published before the calculation` MEANS
            filter (GIVEN revision YIELD revision's `date the figure is published` LESS THAN `date of the calculation`) revisions
        `the latest day` MEANS
            maximum (map (GIVEN revision YIELD Day (revision's `date the figure is published`)) `revisions published before the calculation`)
        `those published on the latest day` MEANS
            filter (GIVEN revision YIELD Day (revision's `date the figure is published`) EQUALS `the latest day`) `revisions published before the calculation`

-- src:539 | Adjustment of Industrial Aggregate
-- src:540 | (7) Where, at any time after the coming into force of this section, a new time or content basis is adopted by Statistics Canada in determining the Industrial Aggregate or the other measure referred to in paragraph (5)(b) for a month and the adoption of that new basis would cause a difference between
-- src:541 | (a) the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30 of any year of the Industrial Aggregate or the other measure referred to in paragraph (5)(b) for each month in that period calculated pursuant to this section on the former time or content basis, as the case may be, and
-- src:542 | (b) the average for that twelve month period of the Industrial Aggregate or the other measure referred to in paragraph (5)(b) for each month in that period calculated pursuant to this section on the new time or content basis, as the case may be,
-- src:543 | of more than one per cent of the average for that twelve month period of the Industrial Aggregate or the other measure referred to in paragraph (5)(b) for each month in that period calculated pursuant to this section on the former time or content basis, the average for that twelve month period calculated on the new time or content basis shall be adjusted by the Minister, on the advice of the Chief Statistician of Canada, to reflect the former time or content basis, and any other averages that are calculated in determining the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year following that twelve month period shall be adjusted accordingly.
-- Where a new time or content basis would change the twelve-month average by more than one per cent, the Minister, on the advice of
-- the Chief Statistician, adjusts the average on the new basis to reflect the former basis, and that adjusted figure is the one used.
@ref Act s 18(7) (src:540-543)
GIVEN `the average for the twelve month period on the former time or content basis` IS A NUMBER
      `the average for that twelve month period on the new time or content basis` IS A NUMBER
      `the average as the Minister, on the advice of the Chief Statistician of Canada, adjusts it to reflect the former basis` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 18(7) — the average to be used for the twelve month period` `the average for the twelve month period on the former time or content basis` `the average for that twelve month period on the new time or content basis` `the average as the Minister, on the advice of the Chief Statistician of Canada, adjusts it to reflect the former basis` MEANS
    IF `the difference` GREATER THAN 1% TIMES `the average for the twelve month period on the former time or content basis`
    THEN `the average as the Minister, on the advice of the Chief Statistician of Canada, adjusts it to reflect the former basis`
    ELSE `the average for that twelve month period on the new time or content basis`
    WHERE
        `the difference` MEANS
            IF `the average for that twelve month period on the new time or content basis` AT LEAST `the average for the twelve month period on the former time or content basis`
            THEN `the average for that twelve month period on the new time or content basis` MINUS `the average for the twelve month period on the former time or content basis`
            ELSE `the average for the twelve month period on the former time or content basis` MINUS `the average for that twelve month period on the new time or content basis`

-- src:544 | Limitation on adjustment
-- src:545 | (8) Subsection (7) shall cease to apply when the Industrial Aggregate or the other measure referred to in paragraph (5)(b) for a month has been calculated on the new time or content basis referred to in that subsection for a period of twenty-four consecutive months ending on June 30 of a year.
@ref Act s 18(8) (src:544-545)
GIVEN `the number of consecutive months ending on June 30 of a year for which the measure has been calculated on the new time or content basis` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 18(8) — subsection (7) has ceased to apply` `the number of consecutive months ending on June 30 of a year for which the measure has been calculated on the new time or content basis` MEANS
    `the number of consecutive months ending on June 30 of a year for which the measure has been calculated on the new time or content basis` AT LEAST 24

§§ `Section 18.1 -- the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings`

-- src:548 | Amount of Year’s Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings
-- src:549 | 18.1 (1) The amount of a Year’s Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings is
-- src:550 | (a) for 2024, 1.07 multiplied by the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year; and
-- src:551 | (b) for 2025 and each subsequent year, 1.14 multiplied by the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year.
-- src:552 | Rounding
-- src:553 | (2) If the amount calculated in accordance with subsection (1) for any year is not a multiple of $100, the Year’s Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year is the amount that is the next multiple of $100 below that amount.
@ref Act s 18.1(1) (src:549-551)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 18.1(1) — the amount calculated for the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings` year `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF year EQUALS 2024 THEN JUST (1.07 TIMES `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year`)
        IF year AT LEAST 2025 THEN JUST (1.14 TIMES `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year`)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref Act s 18.1(2) (src:552-553)
GIVEN `the amount calculated in accordance with subsection (1)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 18.1(2) — the amount rounded down to a multiple of one hundred dollars` `the amount calculated in accordance with subsection (1)` MEANS
    (FLOOR (`the amount calculated in accordance with subsection (1)` DIVIDED BY 100)) TIMES 100

@ref Act s 18.1 (src:548-553)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 18.1 — the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings` year `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 18.1(1) — the amount calculated for the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings` year `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST calculated THEN JUST (`s 18.1(2) — the amount rounded down to a multiple of one hundred dollars` calculated)

§§ `Section 20 -- the Year's Basic Exemption`

-- src:582 | Amount of Year’s Basic Exemption
-- src:583 | 20 (1) Subject to subsection (2), the amount of a Year’s Basic Exemption is the highest multiple of $100 that is less than or equal to 10% of the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year.
-- src:584 | Limitation
-- src:585 | (2) For each year after 1997 the amount of a Year’s Basic Exemption is $3,500.
@ref Act s 20 (src:582-585)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 20 — the Year's Basic Exemption` year `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- (2) For each year after 1997 the amount of a Year's Basic Exemption is $3,500.
        IF year GREATER THAN 1997 THEN JUST 3_500
        -- (1) Subject to subsection (2), the highest multiple of $100 that is less than or equal to 10% of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year.
        -- The Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings begin with 1987 (section 18), so before 1987 the text gives nothing.
        IF year AT LEAST 1987 THEN JUST ((FLOOR ((10% TIMES `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year`) DIVIDED BY 100)) TIMES 100)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Sections 17, 17.1 and 19 (a) to (c) -- a person's own figure for a year`

-- Not a provision: paragraphs (a) to (c) of sections 17, 17.1 and 19 are one text with a different Year's figure and a different
-- keel constructor for paragraph (c). This rule applies them to a base amount.
--   (b) and (c) prevail over (a) ("despite paragraph (a)"); (b) is the year an election of subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) is made or
--   one of paragraph 13(1)(b) is deemed made, and (c) the year one is revoked or deemed revoked.
--   NOTHING: two election events in one year, which the text does not address.
GIVEN facts IS A `cp1 Facts about a person for a year`
      base IS A NUMBER
      `the provision of paragraph (c)` IS A `Provision about reaching an age`
      `paragraphs (b) and (c) are taken into account` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the person's figure prorated under paragraphs (a) to (c)` facts base `the provision of paragraph (c)` `paragraphs (b) and (c) are taken into account` MEANS
    IF `paragraphs (b) and (c) are taken into account` AND `the election event in the year` facts EQUALS `more than one election event in the year`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (base TIMES `the number of months` DIVIDED BY 12)
    WHERE
        year MEANS facts's `the year at hand`
        event MEANS `the election event in the year` facts
        `months excluded by disability` MEANS `the number of months of the year excluded from the contributory period by reason of disability` facts
        `months after seventy or death` MEANS
            `the number of months of the year after the person reaches seventy years of age or dies, whichever is earlier` facts `the provision of paragraph (c)` TRUE
        `the number of months` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `paragraphs (b) and (c) are taken into account` AND event EQUALS `an election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) is made in the year`
                THEN (CONSIDER facts's `date the person makes an election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii)`
                      WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
                      WHEN JUST made THEN max 0 (`the number of months of a year before a first day` year (`s 12(1.1)(b) — the first day on which the election has effect` made) MINUS `months excluded by disability`))
                IF `paragraphs (b) and (c) are taken into account` AND event EQUALS `an election under paragraph 13(1)(b) is deemed made in the year`
                THEN (CONSIDER facts's `month referred to in the election of the person under paragraph 13(1)(b)`
                      WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
                      WHEN JUST election THEN max 0 (`the number of months of a year before a first day` year (`s 13(1.1)(e) — the day on which the election is deemed to be made or revoked` election) MINUS `months excluded by disability`))
                IF `paragraphs (b) and (c) are taken into account` AND event EQUALS `an election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) is revoked in the year`
                THEN (CONSIDER facts's `date the person revokes the election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii)`
                      WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
                      WHEN JUST revoked THEN max 0 (`the number of months of a year from a first day` year (`s 12(1.1)(c) — the first day on which the election ceases to have effect` revoked) MINUS `months after seventy or death`))
                IF `paragraphs (b) and (c) are taken into account` AND event EQUALS `an election under paragraph 13(1)(c) is deemed revoked in the year`
                THEN (CONSIDER facts's `month referred to in the revocation by the person under paragraph 13(1)(c)`
                      WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
                      WHEN JUST revocation THEN max 0 (`the number of months of a year from a first day` year (`s 13(1.1)(e) — the day on which the election is deemed to be made or revoked` revocation) MINUS `months after seventy or death`))
                IF `a paragraph (a) event occurs in the year` facts TRUE
                THEN `the number of months counted under paragraph (a)` facts TRUE
                OTHERWISE 12

§§ `Section 17 -- the maximum pensionable earnings of a person`

-- src:487 | Amount of maximum pensionable earnings
-- src:488 | 17 The amount of the maximum pensionable earnings of a person for a year is the amount of the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings except that,
-- src:489 | (a) for a year in which the person reaches eighteen or seventy years of age or die, in which their contributory period ends under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability or in which a disability pension ceases to be payable to them under this Act or under a provincial pension plan, the amount of the maximum pensionable earnings is equal to that proportion of the amount of the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings that the number of months in the year
-- src:490 | (i) after
-- src:491 | (A) they reach eighteen years of age, or
-- src:492 | (B) the disability pension ceases to be payable, or
-- src:493 | (ii) before
-- src:494 | (A) they reach seventy years of age,
-- src:495 | (B) they die, or
-- src:496 | (C) the month following the month in which their contributory period ends under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability,
-- src:497 | including, if they die, the month in which they die, is of 12;
-- src:498 | (b) despite paragraph (a), for a year in which an election referred to in subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) is made or one referred to in paragraph 13(1)(b) is deemed to be made, the maximum pensionable earnings is equal to that proportion of the amount of the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings that the number of months in the year before the election is made or deemed to be made, as the case may be — minus the number of months that are excluded from the contributory period under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability — is of 12; and
-- src:499 | (c) despite paragraph (a), for a year in which an election referred to in subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) is revoked or one referred to in paragraph 13(1)(c) is deemed to be revoked, the maximum pensionable earnings is equal to that proportion of the amount of the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings that the number of months in the year after the election is revoked or deemed to be revoked, as the case may be — minus the number of months after they reach seventy years of age or die, whichever is earlier — is of 12.
@ref Act s 17 (src:488-499)
GIVEN facts IS A `cp1 Facts about a person for a year`
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 17 — the maximum pensionable earnings of a person for a year` facts `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` MEANS
    `the person's figure prorated under paragraphs (a) to (c)` facts `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` `paragraph 17(c)` TRUE

