§§ `Section 17.1 -- the additional maximum pensionable earnings of a person`

-- src:502 | Amount of additional maximum pensionable earnings
-- src:503 | 17.1 The amount of the additional maximum pensionable earnings of a person for a year is the amount of the Year’s Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings except that,
-- src:504 | (a) for a year in which the person reaches 18 or 70 years of age or dies, in which their contributory period ends under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability or in which a disability pension ceases to be payable to them under this Act or under a provincial pension plan, the amount of the additional maximum pensionable earnings is equal to that proportion of the amount of the Year’s Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings that the number of months in the year
-- src:505 | (i) after
-- src:506 | (A) they reach 18 years of age, or
-- src:507 | (B) the disability pension ceases to be payable, or
-- src:508 | (ii) before
-- src:509 | (A) they reach 70 years of age,
-- src:510 | (B) they die, or
-- src:511 | (C) the month following the month in which their contributory period ends under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability,
-- src:512 | including, if they die, the month in which they die, is of 12;
-- src:513 | (b) despite paragraph (a), for a year in which an election referred to in subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) is made or one referred to in paragraph 13(1)(b) is deemed to be made, the additional maximum pensionable earnings is equal to that proportion of the amount of the Year’s Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings that the number of months in the year before the election is made or deemed to be made, as the case may be — minus the number of months that are excluded from the contributory period under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability — is of 12; and
-- src:514 | (c) despite paragraph (a), for a year in which an election referred to in subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) is revoked or one referred to in paragraph 13(1)(c) is deemed to be revoked, the additional maximum pensionable earnings is equal to that proportion of the amount of the Year’s Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings that the number of months in the year after the election is revoked or deemed to be revoked, as the case may be — minus the number of months after they reach 70 years of age or die, whichever is earlier — is of 12.
@ref Act s 17.1 (src:503-514)
GIVEN facts IS A `cp1 Facts about a person for a year`
      `the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 17.1 — the additional maximum pensionable earnings of a person for a year` facts `the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings` MEANS
    `the person's figure prorated under paragraphs (a) to (c)` facts `the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings` `paragraph 17.1(c)` TRUE

@ref Act s 17.1 (src:503-514)
GIVEN facts IS A `cp1 Facts about a person for a year`
      `the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 17.1 — the additional maximum pensionable earnings of a person for a year, determined without taking into account paragraphs (b) and (c)` facts `the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings` MEANS
    `the person's figure prorated under paragraphs (a) to (c)` facts `the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings` `paragraph 17.1(c)` FALSE

§§ `Section 19 -- the basic exemption of a person`

-- src:557 | 19 The amount of the basic exemption of a person for a year is the amount of the Year’s Basic Exemption except that,
-- src:558 | (a) for a year in which the person reaches eighteen or seventy years of age or die, in which their contributory period ends under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability or in which a disability pension ceases to be payable to them under this Act or under a provincial pension plan, the amount of the basic exemption is equal to that proportion of the amount of the Year’s Basic Exemption that the number of months in the year
-- src:559 | (i) after
-- src:560 | (A) they reach eighteen years of age, or
-- src:561 | (B) the disability pension ceases to be payable, or
-- src:562 | (ii) before
-- src:563 | (A) they reach seventy years of age,
-- src:564 | (B) they die, or
-- src:565 | (C) the month following the month in which their contributory period ends under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability,
-- src:566 | including, if they die, the month in which they die, is of 12;
-- src:567 | (b) despite paragraph (a), for a year in which an election referred to in subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) is made or one referred to in paragraph 13(1)(b) is deemed to be made, the amount of the basic exemption is equal to that proportion of the amount of the Year’s Basic Exemption that the number of months in the year before the election is made or deemed to be made, as the case may be — minus the number of months that are excluded from the contributory period under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability — is of 12;
-- src:568 | (c) despite paragraph (a), for a year in which an election referred to in subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) is revoked or one referred to in paragraph 13(1)(c) is deemed to be revoked, the amount of the basic exemption is equal to that proportion of the amount of the Year’s Basic Exemption that the number of months in the year after the election is revoked or deemed to be revoked, as the case may be — minus the number of months after they reach seventy years of age or die, whichever is earlier — is of 12;
-- src:569 | (d) despite paragraphs (a) to (c), for a year in which a retirement pension becomes payable to them under this Act or under a provincial pension plan, the amount of the basic exemption is equal to that proportion of the amount of the Year’s Basic Exemption that the number of months in the year before the retirement pension becomes payable — minus the number of months that are excluded from the contributory period under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability — is of 12 unless the aggregate of the contributory salary and wages and the contributory self-employed earnings exceeds the amount, adjusted by that proportion, of the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings, in which case, the amount of the basic exemption is increased by the lesser of
-- src:570 | (i) the product obtained by multiplying
-- src:571 | (A) the Year’s Basic Exemption
-- src:572 | by
-- src:573 | (B) one-twelfth of the amount by which the number of months in the year for which a retirement pension is payable exceeds the greater of
-- src:574 | (I) the number of months for which an election referred to in subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) or paragraph 13(1)(b) has effect, and
-- src:575 | (II) the number of months after they reach seventy years of age or die, whichever is earlier, and
-- src:576 | (ii) the amount by which the aggregate of the contributory salary and wages and the contributory self-employed earnings exceeds the product obtained by multiplying
-- src:577 | (A) the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings
-- src:578 | by
-- src:579 | (B) one-twelfth of the amount by which the number of months in the year before the retirement pension becomes payable exceeds the number of months that are excluded from the contributory period under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability.
-- Paragraph (d): for a year in which a retirement pension becomes payable, "despite paragraphs (a) to (c)", the Year's Basic Exemption
-- prorated by the months before it becomes payable (less the months excluded by disability); and, where the aggregate of the
-- contributory salary and wages and the contributory self-employed earnings exceeds the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings adjusted by that
-- proportion, increased by the lesser of (i) and (ii).
@ref Act s 19(d) (src:569-579)
GIVEN facts IS A `cp1 Facts about a person for a year`
      `the Year's Basic Exemption` IS A NUMBER
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate of the contributory salary and wages and the contributory self-employed earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 19(d) — the basic exemption for a year in which a retirement pension becomes payable` facts `the Year's Basic Exemption` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` `the aggregate of the contributory salary and wages and the contributory self-employed earnings` MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `month from which a retirement pension is payable to the person`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST payable THEN
        IF DATE_YEAR payable EQUALS year
        THEN JUST (`the Year's Basic Exemption` TIMES `months before` DIVIDED BY 12 PLUS `the increase`)
        ELSE NOTHING
        WHERE
            year MEANS facts's `the year at hand`
            -- the number of months in the year before the retirement pension becomes payable -- minus the number of months excluded by reason of disability
            `months before` MEANS
                max 0 (`the number of months of a year before a first day` year (`the month of a date` payable)
                       MINUS `the number of months of the year excluded from the contributory period by reason of disability` facts)
            `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings, adjusted by that proportion` MEANS `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` TIMES `months before` DIVIDED BY 12
            `the increase` MEANS
                IF `the aggregate of the contributory salary and wages and the contributory self-employed earnings` GREATER THAN `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings, adjusted by that proportion`
                THEN min `subparagraph (i)` `subparagraph (ii)`
                ELSE 0
            -- (i) the Year's Basic Exemption times one-twelfth of the amount by which the months for which a retirement pension is payable exceed
            -- the greater of (I) the months for which an election has effect and (II) the months after seventy or death, whichever is earlier
            `subparagraph (i)` MEANS
                `the Year's Basic Exemption` TIMES (`the amount by which one amount exceeds another`
                                                         (`the number of months of the year for which a retirement pension is payable` facts)
                                                         (max `months of election` `months after seventy or death`))
                DIVIDED BY 12
            `months of election` MEANS
                count (filter (GIVEN month YIELD
                                   `s 12(1.1) — an election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) has effect in a month` month (facts's `date the person makes an election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii)`) (facts's `date the person revokes the election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii)`)
                                OR `s 13(1.1) — an election under paragraph 13(1)(b) has effect in a month` month (facts's `month referred to in the election of the person under paragraph 13(1)(b)`) (facts's `month referred to in the revocation by the person under paragraph 13(1)(c)`))
                              (`the twelve months of a year` year))
            `months after seventy or death` MEANS
                `the number of months of the year after the person reaches seventy years of age or dies, whichever is earlier` facts `paragraph 19(d)` TRUE
            -- (ii) the amount by which the aggregate exceeds the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings times one-twelfth of the amount by which the months before
            -- the retirement pension becomes payable exceed the months excluded by disability
            `subparagraph (ii)` MEANS
                `the aggregate of the contributory salary and wages and the contributory self-employed earnings` MINUS `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings, adjusted by that proportion`

@ref Act s 19 (src:557-579)
GIVEN facts IS A `cp1 Facts about a person for a year`
      `the Year's Basic Exemption` IS A NUMBER
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate of the contributory salary and wages and the contributory self-employed earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 19 — the basic exemption of a person for a year` facts `the Year's Basic Exemption` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` `the aggregate of the contributory salary and wages and the contributory self-employed earnings` MEANS
    -- (d) applies "despite paragraphs (a) to (c)"
    CONSIDER `s 19(d) — the basic exemption for a year in which a retirement pension becomes payable` facts `the Year's Basic Exemption` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` `the aggregate of the contributory salary and wages and the contributory self-employed earnings`
    WHEN JUST exemption THEN JUST exemption
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the person's figure prorated under paragraphs (a) to (c)` facts `the Year's Basic Exemption` `paragraph 19(c)` TRUE

@ref Act s 19 (src:557-579)
GIVEN facts IS A `cp1 Facts about a person for a year`
      `the Year's Basic Exemption` IS A NUMBER
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate of the contributory salary and wages and the contributory self-employed earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 19 — the basic exemption of a person for a year, determined without taking into account paragraphs (b) and (c)` facts `the Year's Basic Exemption` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` `the aggregate of the contributory salary and wages and the contributory self-employed earnings` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 19(d) — the basic exemption for a year in which a retirement pension becomes payable` facts `the Year's Basic Exemption` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` `the aggregate of the contributory salary and wages and the contributory self-employed earnings`
    WHEN JUST exemption THEN JUST exemption
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the person's figure prorated under paragraphs (a) to (c)` facts `the Year's Basic Exemption` `paragraph 19(c)` FALSE

§§ `Section 16 -- the maximum contributory earnings of a person`

-- src:483 | Amount of maximum contributory earnings for a year
-- src:484 | 16 The amount of the maximum contributory earnings of a person for a year is the amount of his maximum pensionable earnings for the year, minus the amount of his basic exemption for the year.
@ref Act s 16 (src:483-484)
GIVEN `the amount of the person's maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the person's basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 16 — the maximum contributory earnings of a person for a year` `the amount of the person's maximum pensionable earnings for the year` `the amount of the person's basic exemption for the year` MEANS
    `the amount of the person's maximum pensionable earnings for the year` MINUS `the amount of the person's basic exemption for the year`
